  "$comment": "THE one list of what the data views show by default that the data sync prepares as columns (so a page reads stored columns by key and never works a value out of a JSON document). Read by the web app (embedded; ViewStoredColumns.cs) AND by the data sync (engine/pro-data/_shared/SI-DataViewContext.ps1 reads THIS file). To add a field: add ONE entry here, and its guarded column (and index, when indexed) in sql/si-data-schema.sql -- a test names the line that is missing. 'ci': key = the layout key (ci.f.<CI document field> | ci.i.<identifier type> | ci.links), column = the sidata.Ci column, type = NVARCHAR(n) (n <= 4000; a scalar text field) | INT / FLOAT (a number) | BIT (yes / no) | DATETIME2(3) (a date, UTC) | JSON (a list / object field, kept as its JSON text) | LIST (identifier values or linked object ids, '; '-joined), indexed = an index on the column (IX_Ci_<column>), filter = 'values' when the CI grid filters the column by its values (a short closed vocabulary). 'finding': key = the finding context key (fc.*), column = the sidata.Finding column, issue = the sidata.IssueContext column (one row per collection + CVE / issue), type = NVARCHAR(n) | NVARCHAR(MAX) (a text nothing may cut: description, remediation, evidence) | INT / FLOAT | DATETIME2(3) -- on the per-issue row a text is the distinct values, a number the highest and a date the earliest over the key's findings -- fields = the names the value is read under in the finding's row (first one that has a value), flags = a yes / no column made of flags. A changed list is picked up by the next data sync on its own: every CI is filled once more (no CI build needed) and every collection is prepared once more (sidata.Ci.CtxSet / sidata.Collection.ContextSet carry the list they were filled for).",
